      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I can provide you with some general guidelines for identifying potential high-risk guest profiles. These profiles can be categorized into three main groups: High-Risk, Medium-Risk, and Low-Risk. High-Risk profiles may include guests with a history of violent or aggressive behavior, prominent or notorious individuals, those traveling with large sums of cash or jewelry, and guests who appear intoxicated or overly aggressive upon arrival. \n\nMedium-Risk profiles may include guests who appear disheveled or suspicious, are traveling alone, or have an unusual or unclear purpose for their stay. Low-Risk profiles are typically guests who are well-dressed, appear calm and composed, and have a clear reason for their stay.",
